":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"C061\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Lists the board of trustees, investment adviser, distributor, custodian, administrator/fund accounting, transfer agent and auditor.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Covers APs, liquidity providers/market makers, exchange listing, DTC/NSCC clearing and creation/redemption processing, which roughly matches the PCF workflow. Seed capital is not mentioned.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Includes legal counsel and pricing vendors. Index provider/licensing is tied to index-tracking funds and the securities lending agent to 'if lending'.\"},{\"point\":4,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Says service providers are 'often bundled' and that 'One provider can often cover several of these'. The adviser may house the CCO and valuation designee.\"},{\"point\":5,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Names a chief compliance officer under Rule 38a-1 and a majority-independent board with Section 15(c) review, which covers the compliance program and board oversight.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"Required coverage totals 4.5 of 5, with no central error. The answer explicitly rejects the idea that each role needs a separate firm. Listing the Rule 22e-4 liquidity program as strategy-specific is imprecise, since ETFs generally need one, but the 'if applicable' hedge keeps it short of a material falsehood. The only gap is seed capital, which leaves point 2 incomplete, so not every required minimum is covered and the grade cannot be correct.\"}","ttft_ms":5043,"type":"result","duration_ms":9533,"uuid":"e8349b6e-17d6-4e71-ab14-175a9b32ba2e","ttft_stream_ms":1071,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":1071,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
